    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "No, an [On Deletion] effect activates after the card is moved to the trash. Therefore, the card is first sent to the trash.",
        "question": "If I use this card's [On Deletion] effect to return this card to the hand, does it mean that this card isn't sent to the trash?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, it cannot be activated. Until the first occurrence of the first process is resolved, all immediate/interruptive effects can be activated only once each. In this situation, until the first Sukamon A deletion resolves, each of the \"When X would\" effects can only be activated once, so Sukamon A that has already been activated cannot be activated again.",
        "question": "There are \"Sukamon\" A and \"Sukamon\" B in the Battle Area, both of which have this card as their digivolution card. When \"Sukamon\" A was about to be deleted, it tried to delete \"Sukamon\" B with this card's inherited effect. On the other hand, when \"Sukamon\" B is about to be deleted, it tried to delete \"Sukamon\" A with this card's inherited effect. In this case, can \"Sukamon\" A activate this card's inherited effect again?",
        "reference": "[2]"
      }
    ]
  },
